Organizations worldwide would say that some form of espionage is a must to =
gain that much-needed edge over the competition. In fact, surveillance soft=
ware in its various forms has created a multibillion-dollar industry. But s=
ome, like Predator, may be taking espionage too far.

WhoisXML API researchers, aided by WHOIS, IP, and DNS tools, took an in-dep=
th look at Predator's digital footprint to find out if it is indeed legal a=
s it touts to be. Our investigation on 21 email addresses belonging to Pred=
ator's creator Cytrox led to the discovery of additional artifacts that cou=
ld have ties to the Predator infrastructure, reiterating its malicious natu=
re.

